  "r9Notes": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 420,
   "fill": "yellow",
   "page": "round9",
   "text": "Round 9: Settings, all in one modal (1080 × 680) over a dimmed shell page. Section URLs (/settings/staff) open the modal on that section; Esc or × closes it.\n\nNav by permission, hidden not locked: technician = Account only (row 1); Lab Manager = Account, Lab, Concrete Equipment + Suppliers; administrator = everything, incl. Holidays, Report header and System.\n\nAdmin sections are wide panels: header with the main action, TableToolbar, Table; rows open the Inbox drawer (PeekSplit) to edit. Destructive changes ask for a reason (Disable access, Retire location).\n\nAt 1024 px the modal fills the window less a 16 px margin and the nav narrows to 192 px; drawer lists hide columns by container width.\n\nLocations carry a Storage term (Short-term / Long-term); a stored unit's lifecycle step follows its location.\n\nGates stay open items: G8 units/methods (Equipment), report templates (Report header). No session settings (D38).\n\nToasts are drawn as static Sonner mock-ups inside the modal."
  },
  "splitAbout": {
   "x": -560,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 420,
   "fill": "blue",
   "page": "round7",
   "text": "Strata, part 2: rounds 7 (concrete lab), 8 (concrete review and reports) and 9 (settings). Everything else (shell, components, sign in, Today, Inbox, rounds 1–6 and 10) is on the main canvas, Material Mule — Strata. Split on 2026-11-12 because one canvas holds at most 512 files. The Shared shell page holds copies of the shell and Today pages these boards sit on; change them on the main canvas. All data is fictional."
  }
